MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Grass Roots, Neil Diamond, and Chronicle fit my recent interest in older pop and classic-rock hits that I can enjoy repeatedly.",
    "The Beatles recommendation connects directly to my interest in Sgt. Pepper's, while Elvis 30 #1 Hits offers the familiar songs I am seeking in a compilation."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Travis Tritt's country collection does not fit the older pop and classic rock I want today, even though it is another best-of album.",
    "Dances With Wolves offers a film score when I want songs and singers, and This One's from the Heart gives me too little recognizable musical context to choose it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A greatest-hits label alone is not enough for me; the artist and kind of music still need to fit my current listening interests.",
    "My interest in older recordings does not mean every older release feels equally relevant, especially a soundtrack or a different style of music."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated interest in compilations reflects a desire for recognizable, melodic songs, which makes familiar artists more compelling than an era match alone such as the Tymes.",
    "I distinguish between familiar songs and new versions: the Beatles live album interests me because of my Beatles listening, but I would choose straightforward Elvis hits before the orchestral reinterpretations."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations mostly understood my interest in familiar older pop and classic-rock collections, but sometimes treated an era or compilation format as enough to match my mood."
}
